Wide World Importers - End-to-End Sales Performance Analytics & Diagnostic Study

Project Overview

This project delivers an end-to-end Business Intelligence solution for Wide World Importers, transforming raw transactional data into actionable strategic insights. The core objective extends beyond descriptive metrics to conduct a deep diagnostic analysis of sales trends, revenue trajectory, product dynamics, and customer retention patterns.

The analytical workflow encompasses an enterprise-grade ETL process using Power Query, a Star Schema data model optimized for performance, complex DAX computations including Time-Intelligence functions, and an interactive dashboard built in Power BI.

Business Problem & Diagnostic Hypothesis

Primary Observed Issue

While aggregate sales figures demonstrate absolute baseline growth year-over-year (reaching a baseline of 45M in 2013 and adding 4.9M in 2014), the net compound growth rate remains significantly below target capacity.

Diagnostic Breakdown

Product Level: Sales performance across Stock Items remains consistently positive with normal variance. Product performance is not the root cause of slow growth.
Geographic Level: Regional distribution shows strong sales velocity, specifically within top-performing states such as Texas.
Customer Retention (Root Cause): Longitudinal analysis of Top 10 customer cohorts reveals a high churn and drop-off rate. Top-tier accounts in 2013 experienced reduced purchasing volumes or disappeared entirely from top ranks in 2014 and 2015, replaced by new accounts rather than recurring organic expansion.
Seasonal Volatility: MoM analysis highlights recurring revenue contractions during February and August (end of Q1 and Q3 transition), impacting momentum into subsequent quarters.
Data Pipeline & ETL Architecture (Power Query)

Fact Table Optimization (
Fact_Sales)

Header & Type Standardizations: Corrected initial structural misalignments and explicit data typing across all numeric and textual attributes.
Tax Rate Normalization: Transformed Tax Rate values originally stored as whole numbers by applying integer-to-decimal transformation (Value / 100) and configuring explicit percentage data typing to enable accurate revenue calculations.
2. Dimension Clean-up & Transformation

Dim_StockItem: Standardized missing values by replacing n/a entries in color attributes with Unknown. Executed row filters to purge redundant metadata records.
Dim_Customer: Applied advanced string extraction routines (Text After Delimiter) to eliminate redundant attributes shared across Customer, Bill To Customer, and Buying Group columns, resolving data duplication and ensuring dimensional uniqueness.
Dim_City & Dim_Date: Purged unneeded records, standardized headers, and established primary surrogate key structures.
Data Modeling Strategy

The semantic layer is structured using a strict Star Schema centered around Fact_Sales to ensure optimized query execution and clear dimensional filtering pathways.

